{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Your name shall no longer be called Jacob.</b> At the end of days, when you shall endure after the destruction of the nations — and by then the matter of <b>Jacob</b>, which denotes enduring at the end, will already be fulfilled in you — therefore the name <b>Jacob</b> will no longer fall upon you then, to indicate that you will be at the heel and at the end of all the nations." "<b>But Israel, for you have striven.</b> But they shall call you by the name Israel alone, to indicate that by then you have already striven <b>with Elohim, etc.</b>, in the manner of (Isaiah 24:21): \"יפקד יהוה על צבא המרום במרום ועל מלכי האדמה על האדמה.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Reading לְקֵץ הַיָּמִין as לְקֵץ הַיָּמִין (end of days) per context; the form is unusual and could conceivably be a typographical variant, but the sense is clear."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:05.561540784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}